# Repository continuity

Detail: [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) sections "Where development happens" and "Session routine". IP rules: [docs/policies/INTELLECTUAL_PROPERTY.md](../../docs/policies/INTELLECTUAL_PROPERTY.md). Workflow: [docs/handoffs/MULTI_MACHINE_WORKFLOW.md](../../docs/handoffs/MULTI_MACHINE_WORKFLOW.md).

- Develop only through Cursor on the Fedora laptop or the Bazzite desktop. Stop if the checkout is `/agent/repos/NES_Plus` or the user is `ubuntu` in a cloud agent path.
- Fedora sole checkout: `/home/g/Desktop/NES_Plus`. The path `/home/g/Desktop/CURSOR/nes_plus` is obsolete. Do not create sibling Nesticles clones.
- Bazzite: one checkout under `/home/UltraMagnus69r` (exact subdirectory verified on that machine). Do not copy trees by hand between machines.
- The canonical remote is https://github.com/UltraMagnus69r/NES_Plus. Start with `./scripts/session-start.sh`. When origin is ahead and the tree is clean, fast-forward **this directory**. Finish a substantial session with a push whose remote SHA matches HEAD.
- Do not commit ROMs, extracted commercial art, commercial audio, secrets, UNKNOWN assets, or the Godot executable. Run `./scripts/check-repository-safety.sh --staged`.
- Do not force-push. Do not merge to `main` unless the owner asks. Do not hard-reset as the way to sync. Never discard local work merely to match GitHub.
